#: R/texts.R
msgid ""
"Common misreading: a few Hij below .30 are not a problem by themselves; the "
".30 criterion applies to Hi and H. What matters at the pair level is the "
"sign."
msgstr ""

#: R/texts.R
msgid ""
"Common misreading: a scale can be perfectly usable without IIO. To order "
"respondents by the total score, what matters is the monotone homogeneity "
"model (one attribute, local independence and monotonicity); IIO is an "
"additional requirement only when the order of the items itself is "
"interpreted."
msgstr ""

#: R/texts.R
msgid ""
"Common misreading: a selected scale is not yet a validated scale. The "
"selection only guarantees scalability; monotonicity, invariant item ordering "
"and the theoretical coherence of the items still have to be checked."
msgstr ""

#: R/texts.R
msgid ""
"Common misreading: an outlier is a signal to inspect, not a reason to "
"delete. Unusual patterns can come from careless responding, but also from "
"respondents for whom the attribute works differently, and removing them "
"changes what the scale means."
msgstr ""

#: R/texts.R
msgid ""
"Common misreading: H is not a reliability coefficient and not a correlation. "
"A long scale can be very reliable (high alpha) and still have weak "
"scalability, because reliability rewards the number of items while H "
"measures how consistently they order people."
msgstr ""

