"al., 2010). Below .30 inaccurate, .30-.40 weak, .40-.50 medium, .50 or "
"higher high."
msgstr ""

#: R/texts.R
msgid ""
"HT summarizes how accurately the remaining items are ordered: below .30 the "
"order is too inaccurate to use, .30 to .40 weak, .40 to .50 medium, .50 or "
"more high (Ligtvoet et al., 2010). Report HT only after the backward "
"selection has removed violating items."
msgstr ""

#: R/texts.R
msgid ""
"HW (within) is the ordinary scalability computed on each rater's own item "
"scores: it tells whether every rater uses the items consistently. HB "
"(between) uses item scores of different raters of the same subject: it tells "
"whether the items order the subjects consistently across raters. For a scale "
"that measures subjects, HB is the coefficient that matters most."
msgstr ""

