#: R/texts.R
msgid ""
"In a unidimensional monotone model, each inter-item correlation must lie "
"between bounds derived from the other items (Ellis, 2014; see references). "
"L1 and U1 overestimate the lower and upper bound, L2 and U2 underestimate "
"them, so a correlation below L2 or above U1 is a clear violation and one "
"below L1 or above U2 only a possible one."
msgstr ""

#: R/texts.R
msgid ""
"In the plot, curves should rise from left to right. Small dips within the "
"confidence band are sampling noise; a clear, sustained fall is a real "
"violation."
msgstr ""

#: R/texts.R
msgid ""
"In the plot, each line is one item step: lines of P(++) should only go down "
"and lines of P(--) only go up."
