#: R/texts.R
msgid ""
"Local independence is checked through three special cases of conditional "
"association (Holland & Rosenbaum, 1986; see references): covariances between "
"items must not be negative conditional on sum scores of other items. The "
"worst offending item is removed and the check repeated, until no item is "
"flagged (Straat et al., 2016; see references)."
msgstr ""

#: R/texts.R
msgid ""
"Local independence means that, once the attribute is taken into account, "
"item responses are unrelated. Locally dependent items (for example, items "
"sharing a stimulus or almost identical wording) inflate scalability and "
"reliability."
msgstr ""

